# Files Git should leave alone.

# `node_modules` here is not a real folder — it's a leftover shortcut
# pointing at a temporary location that no longer exists. Git can't open
# it, which is what produced:
#     error: open("node_modules"): Function not implemented
#     fatal: Unable to process path node_modules
# Nothing in this app needs it: index.html loads plain HTML/CSS/JS with no
# build step, and the three dev scripts (test_engine.js, test_data_layer.js,
# qa_check.js) all run on plain `node` with nothing installed.
node_modules

# Windows / macOS folder clutter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# The original 3440x1440 background PNGs, if you ever put them back in this
# folder. The app loads the resized bg-1.jpg ... bg-6.jpg instead (1.45 MB
# for all six, versus about 37 MB for the originals).
assets/Backgrounds/*.png
